KZ3 patch 2099 (RSX pass 94): PC-style mouse look sensitivity, a frame-stamped look accumulator, and a D3D12 WARP
fallback (the RE notes "Pass 94").
libs/input/pad_mouse.{h,c}: sensitivity = user factor (KZ3_MOUSE_SENS, default 2.5) x degrees per count
(KZ3_MOUSE_YAW, default 0.022 = Quake/Source m_yaw) -> 0.055 deg/count, no acceleration, no smoothing; ADS keeps the
weapon's own factor times KZ3_MOUSE_ZOOM_SENS; kz3.ini [input] keys mouse_sensitivity / mouse_ads_sensitivity /
mouse_invert_y (table pad_mouse_ini_keys, read by port/kz3/main.cpp). The accumulator (PadLookAcc, pure) stamps adds
and takes with the guest frame (cellGcm_flip_request_count): with no take in the last 4 frames only the current
frame's counts are kept, so the first look update after a menu, pause, cutscene or load no longer gets the mouse
travel of the whole break (Windows hand test: d=-3665,-1057 in the first on-foot update); a stall keeps every count.
libs/video/rsx_d3d12_device.h (new): rsx_d3d12_create_device: the default adapter as before, WARP
(IDXGIFactory4::EnumWarpAdapter) only when that gives no device, RSX_D3D12_WARP=1 forces WARP, =0 never; one
"[d3d12] device" line (adapter, vendor, software, max feature level, binding tier, highest shader model).
rsx_live_draw.c and rsx_d3d12_backend.c create their device through it. Host tests tools/smoke/test_mouse_look.sh,
tools/smoke/test_d3d12_warp.sh.

